{{~##
   What every generated Python module starts with: the banner and the imports.

   Every module gets the same three standard library imports, and Python does not object to
   one it does not use - it is not even a warning. Go could not do this; the difference is
   worth stating, because from here the two look identical.

   `imports` is what this file actually needs from its siblings, worked out by
   TypeDependencies. Relative, so the package is importable from wherever it is dropped
   rather than only from a path something has to set first.

   Ends two blank lines before whatever declares itself next, which is what PEP 8 asks for
   ahead of a top level class.
##~}}
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by Tabbit. DO NOT EDIT.
#
# Changes to this file may cause incorrect behavior and will be lost if the code is
# regenerated.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

import enum
import os

from . import tabbit
{{~ for line in imports ~}}
{{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}


